#
# Linux for the Cora Z7-07S's processing system, beside the CADR in its fabric.
#
#     make buildroot-cora     # from the repository root; see the Makefile
#
# What comes out (output/images/): boot.bin (U-Boot's SPL, the first-stage
# loader that runs the start-up routine), u-boot.img, zImage,
# zynq-cora-z7-07s.dtb, rootfs.cpio.uboot.  The first two go on the card with
# uEnv.txt; the rest are served by TFTP or read off the card.
#
# **IT NEEDS BOTH EXTERNAL TREES**, because the packages live in the Arty
# Z7-20's and this one holds only the board:
#
#     BR2_EXTERNAL=boards/arty-z7-20/linux/buildroot:boards/cora-z7-07s/linux/buildroot
#
# `$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_PATH)` below is that first tree and
# `$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_CORA_PATH)` this one, and which of the two a line names
# is the whole of what is shared and what is this board's.
#
# **NOTHING BUILT FROM THIS HAS RUN.**  No Cora Z7-07S has been booted from
# this repository and this configuration has not been built here; what holds
# it is that it is the Arty Z7-20's, which has booted, with the differences
# below and no others.
#
# Everything is pinned: Buildroot by version and sha256 in the Makefile, and
# through it U-Boot 2026.01 and Linux 6.19.14 by the hashes Buildroot itself
# carries, checked on download because BR2_DOWNLOAD_FORCE_CHECK_HASHES is set.
# The downloads live in vendor/buildroot-dl, shared with the other board's
# build, so a rebuild does not refetch.

BR2_arm=y
BR2_cortex_a9=y
BR2_ARM_ENABLE_NEON=y
BR2_ARM_ENABLE_VFP=y
BR2_DL_DIR="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_PATH)/../../../../vendor/buildroot-dl"
BR2_DOWNLOAD_FORCE_CHECK_HASHES=y

# **ONE CORTEX-A9 AND THE TOOLCHAIN DOES NOT CARE.**  The XC7Z007S has one
# core where the XC7Z020 has two; it is the same Cortex-A9 with the same NEON
# and the same VFP, so the architecture lines above are the other board's
# unchanged.  What knows about the core count is the device tree, which
# disables cpu1.
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN=y
BR2_TOOLCHAIN_EXTERNAL_BOOTLIN_ARMV7_EABIHF_GLIBC_STABLE=y

# The board on a private LAN: root with the password the other board
# documents, over Dropbear, with the address from DHCP.
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_HOSTNAME="cadr"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ISSUE="the Cora Z7-07S beside the CADR"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_ROOT_PASSWD="root"
BR2_SYSTEM_DHCP="eth0"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_PORT="ttyPS0"
BR2_TARGET_GENERIC_GETTY_BAUDRATE_115200=y

# The kernel: mainline, the version Buildroot pins, with the OTHER BOARD's
# config file and this board's device tree.
#
# **THE KERNEL CONFIG IS SHARED AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.**  It names what a
# Zynq-7000 with a UART, a gigabit MAC, an SD controller and a USB host
# controller needs, and Digilent gives both boards that same set of
# peripherals on the same MIO pins.  The one peripheral the two do not share
# is Quad SPI, which this board's processing system has disabled: an MTD
# driver for a device the pin multiplexing never routes is inert, and a second
# copy of a 150-line kernel configuration is a second thing to keep current.
# If the two ever want different kernels, this line is where they part.
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_USE_CUSTOM_CONFIG=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_CONFIG_FILE="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_PATH)/board/arty-z7-20/linux/linux.config"
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_ZIMAGE=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_DTS_SUPPORT=y
BR2_LINUX_KERNEL_CUSTOM_DTS_DIR="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_CORA_PATH)/board/cora-z7-07s/dts"

# The root filesystem: BusyBox (devmem, udhcpc, init), Dropbear, and our own
# programs.  An initramfs as a U-Boot ramdisk image, so the card holds no
# filesystem.
BR2_PACKAGE_DROPBEAR=y
BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_CONSOLE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_READOUT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_CHECKPOINT=y
BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_DISK_PACKS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_TERMINAL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_SERIAL=y
BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_CHAOSNET=y
BR2_PACKAGE_MUIR=y

# **THREE THINGS THE ARTY Z7-20's IMAGE HAS AND THIS ONE DOES NOT**, and all
# three are one decision: there is no USB input on this board.
#
#   `BR2_PACKAGE_CADR_USB_INPUT`  the program that reads evdev devices at the
#                                 board and hands their events to
#                                 `cadr-terminal`.  A keyboard and a mouse
#                                 reach the machine from a VIEWER here, over
#                                 the network, which is what `cadr-terminal`
#                                 does on both boards and is the only way in
#                                 on this one.
#   `BR2_PACKAGE_EVTEST`          the tool that prints what a
#                                 `/dev/input/event*` node delivers.  It is in
#                                 the other image to prove the USB port on the
#                                 board, and there is nothing here to prove.
#   `BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY`          the other board's overlay is one init
#                                 script, `S15usbvbus`, which tells the USB
#                                 PHY to drive VBUS so a device on the host
#                                 port gets power.  With no program reading a
#                                 USB device, powering the port is a write to
#                                 a PHY for no reason.
#
# The device tree still declares `usb0` as a host, because the port exists and
# Digilent's own tree for this board declares it; a board that later wants USB
# input takes the package, `evtest` and the VBUS script together and nothing
# in the fabric or the tree changes.
#
# **THE MACHINE LOSES NOTHING BY IT.**  The I/O board's keyboard and mouse
# registers are on `M_AXI_GP0` here exactly as they are there, and
# `cadr-terminal` is the one program that writes them on either board.

# The other board's post-build script, unchanged, and that is deliberate: it
# asserts that the image holds only the programs the packages install, and the
# packages are that tree's.  Buildroot builds output/target/ up and never
# removes what a package stopped installing, so a renamed package leaves its
# old program and its old init script in the image beside the new ones.  That
# happened once and two disk pack programs ran on a board writing blocks back
# to the same pack.
BR2_ROOTFS_POST_BUILD_SCRIPT="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_PATH)/board/arty-z7-20/post-build.sh"
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_CPIO=y
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_CPIO_GZIP=y
BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_CPIO_UIMAGE=y
# BR2_TARGET_ROOTFS_TAR is not set

# U-Boot: mainline, the generic Zynq configuration with our fragment over it,
# our device tree, and SPL as the first-stage loader running the start-up
# routine generated from boards/cora-z7-07s/vivado/ps7_init.ops.  The three
# dts files are copied into arch/arm/dts/ before the build; the -u-boot.dtsi
# is picked up by name.  The reserved-memory dtsi is the OTHER tree's, because
# the CADR's memory map is a property of the machine and not of the board.
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_BUILD_SYSTEM_KCONFIG=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_VERSION=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_VERSION_VALUE="2026.01"
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_BOARD_DEFCONFIG="xilinx_zynq_virt"
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CONFIG_FRAGMENT_FILES="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_CORA_PATH)/board/cora-z7-07s/uboot/uboot.fragment"
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_NEEDS_DTC=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_NEEDS_OPENSSL=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_NEEDS_GNUTLS=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_FORMAT_IMG=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_SPL=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_SPL_NAME="spl/boot.bin"
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_ZYNQ=y
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_ZYNQ_PS7_INIT_FILE="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_CORA_PATH)/board/cora-z7-07s/uboot/ps7_init_gpl.c"
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_DTS_PATH="$(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_CORA_PATH)/board/cora-z7-07s/dts/xilinx/zynq-cora-z7-07s.dts $(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_CORA_PATH)/board/cora-z7-07s/uboot/zynq-cora-z7-07s-u-boot.dtsi $(BR2_EXTERNAL_CADR_PATH)/../cadr-reserved.dtsi"
BR2_TARGET_UBOOT_CUSTOM_MAKEOPTS="DEVICE_TREE=zynq-cora-z7-07s"

# For the card image boards/cora-z7-07s/linux/mksd-buildroot.sh writes at
# staging time, when the TFTP server's address is known.
BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_DOSFSTOOLS=y
BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_GENIMAGE=y
BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_MTOOLS=y
